From: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: phy: as2xxxx: keep DPC rate adaptation on for the AN8831

The v2.5.3 driver maps phylink in-band negotiation to the DPC rate
adaptation. phylink calls config_inband(LINK_INBAND_DISABLE) for an
out-of-band PHY link, so the rate adaptation that config_init enables is
switched off again and a copper link below 10G passes no frames over the
10G USXGMII host link (BPI-R4 Pro 8X Combo LAN behind MxL862xx port 5:
1G link up, rx_packets 0). Keep it on for the AN8831, as v1.x did.

Signed-off-by: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/phy/as2xxxx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/as2xxxx.c
@@ -2684,8 +2684,15 @@
 		return 0;
 
 	if (phydev->phy_id == PHY_ID_AS21XXX_AN8831) {
-		/* no care speed*/
-		ret = aeon_ipc_dpc_ra_set(phydev, en, 0);
+		/*
+		 * On the AN8831 the DPC rate adaptation is what lets a 1G/2.5G/5G
+		 * copper link run over the fixed 10G USXGMII host link, and
+		 * aeon_config_init() enables it. phylink calls config_inband()
+		 * with LINK_INBAND_DISABLE for an out-of-band PHY link, which
+		 * switched the rate adaptation off again: below 10G nothing was
+		 * received. Keep it on, as the v1.x driver did.
+		 */
+		return 0;
 	} else if (phydev->phy_id == PHY_ID_AS22XXX_AN8833) {
 		ret = aeon_ipc_dpc_ra_set(phydev, en, speed);
 	} else {
